rengths:<br\/><br\/><strong>1. Coach Style<\/strong>- It is used to convey what an idea is instead of communicating how it can happen.<br\/><strong>2.<\/strong> <strong>Freeform Style- <\/strong>It involves loose structure and stories and is ideal for short presentations.<br\/><strong>3. Connector Style- <\/strong>It shows to the audience how similar a presenter is to them, ensuring better connection. It allows the presenter to learn and grow with the audience.<br\/><strong>4. Visual Style- <\/strong>It involves heavy use of images to get across a point.<br\/><strong>5. Storytelling Style- <\/strong>It includes anecdotes and examples that connect you emotionally with the audience.<br\/><strong>6. Instructor Style- <\/strong>It is mainly used for lectures in universities to impart information to the audience.<br\/><strong>7. Lessig Style- <\/strong>It is used for short and concise presentations, where you talk about each slide for no longer than 15 seconds.\u00a0<br\/><strong>8. Takahashi Style- <\/strong>It uses plain and large texts on slides. There are no images and just 1-2 sentences. It is used when you are short on time and must get straight to the point.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192295938\",\"position\":2,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192295938\",\"name\":\"What makes a good presentation?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"A good presentation ensures more audience engagement, interaction, and participation. It should convey your thoughts and ideas clearly and be well-researched. Also, you must have the necessary knowledge of the topic and must speak confidently.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192314658\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192314658\",\"name\":\"How can I be less nervous during a presentation?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The following are a few tips to be less nervous during your presentation:<br\/> -Stay focused on what you say rather than on your audience because people are more interested in what you have to say.<br\/> -Stay organized and confident, so you know what to say and when. You should know your content by heart.<br\/> -If you forget a point or lose track of your presentation, do not fear silence. Use it as a chance to take a deep breath and get back on track.<br\/> -Practice multiple times before the final presentation.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192350395\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192350395\",\"name\":\"What are some important actions to take before the presentation?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Before you give your final presentation, take the following steps to ensure everything goes smoothly:<br\/> -Arrive early<br\/> -Get familiar with the room<br\/> -Listen to other presenters<br\/> -Use note cards\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192374349\",\"position\":5,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/presentation-skills\/#faq-question-1716192374349\",\"name\":\"Why should I develop public speaking skills?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Here are the major benefits of public speaking skills:<br\/> -Helps in career and personal growth.<br\/> -Allows you to share your ideas confidently with people.<br\/>